   158	
   159	## Results
   160	
   161	A  total  of  37  407  healthy  individuals  from  87  datasets from  20  countries  were  included  in  this  study.  This sample consisted of 19 964 females and 17 443 males.
   162	
   163	The MAE, RMSE, explained variance, and CPU time of the models for the left thalamic volume and left medial orbitofrontal cortical thickness and surface area in females are shown as exemplars (figure 2; the corresponding data for males is in appendix 1 p 4). The pattern  was  the  same  for  all  regions  across  sex-specific models  (appendix  1  pp  5-6;  appendix  3).  Across  all models, the OLSR and MFPR had the shortest CPU times (less than 1 s) whereas GPR had the longest (25-60 min). Across  all  sex-specific  and  region-specific  models,  the LMS, GPR, WBLR, and MFPR had comparable values for MAE, RMSE, and explained variance that were statistically better at P FDR &lt;0·05 than those for GAMLSS, BLR, OLSR, and  HBR.  Accordingly,  the  MFPR  emerged  as  the preferred  algorithm  given  its  combined  advantages  in accuracy and computational e/uniFB03ciency.
